{
  "_README": [
    "Fixture: a flawed Mendix domain model, hand-built in the normalised shape.",
    "",
    "Hand-built rather than scraped because Mendix has no stable text export of a",
    "domain model, and a fixture that depends on one version's HTML markup would rot",
    "silently. This is also the shape a reviewer should build when the HTML adapter",
    "comes up thin: honest and complete beats scraped and partial.",
    "",
    "The point of this fixture is the paradigm boundary. Every relational key and",
    "integrity rule is NOT_APPLICABLE here, and the Mendix substitutes fire instead:",
    "identity is a Unique validation rule, requiredness is a Required validation rule,",
    "orphan risk is delete behaviour, audit is system members, and PascalCase is",
    "correct rather than a violation.",
    "",
    "_expected_to_fire is read by selftest.py."
  ],
